## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
extended-nh-encoding [ label-ipv4 ] [ vpn-ipv4 ]
no extended-nh-encoding
FuncDef:
This command configures BGP to advertise (at session OPEN) the capability to receive label IPv4, VPN IPv4 routes, or IPv6 next hops from the peers. These peers should not send such routes unless they receive notification of this capability. If the SR OS router receives a label IPv4 or VPN IPv4 route from a peer to which it did not advertise the necessary capability, the UPDATE message will be considered malformed and this will cause either session reset ortreat-as-withdrawbehavior depending on the error handling settings.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'label-ipv4', 'Info': 'Instructs BGP to advertise an extended NH encoding capability for NLRI AFI=1, NLRI SAFI=4, and next-hop AFI=2.'}
{'Parameters': 'vpn-ipv4', 'Info': 'Instructs BGP to advertise an extended NH encoding capability for NLRI AFI=1, NLRI SAFI=128, and next-hop AFI=2.'}
